_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 8
---
order: 8
---
short_label: XII.8
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Similar pyramids with triangular bases are in triplicate ratio of their corresponding sides.
----
proof:

Let there be similar and similarly situated pyramids with triangular bases *AB* and {DEF} vertices {G} and {H}.

I say that the pyramid {ABCG|pABCG} has to the pyramid {DEFH|pDEFH} the ratio triplicate of that which {BC} has to {EF}.

Complete the parallelepipedal solids *BGML* and *EHQP.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="440" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.8 diagram" src="propXII8.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The pyramids are given; the one construction is completing the two
    // parallelepipeds, after which the walk is highlight beats.
    //
    // A polyhedron draws no highlight, so the two pyramids get faceless
    // wireframe twins, octagons that walk all six edges (pABCG, pDEFH;
    // prose refs use the display override). The solids BGML and EHQP are
    // lit through their six faces; the prism that is half of BGML (bases
    // ABC and KGN) through its five. Every added element is transparent,
    // so the resting figure is unchanged.
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): B, E, F (lineSliders) are
    // givens; M (lineSlider) and N (planeSlider) arrive only when the solids
    // are completed, so they are deferred. Every other point is derived.
    var PYR   = ["A","B","C","G","D","E","F","H","ABCG","DEFH",
                 "AB","BC","BG","DE","EF","EH","ABC","DEF","pABCG","pDEFH"];
    var SOLID = ["M","N","K","L","Q'","Q","R","O","P",
                 "GNLK","HRPO","KAML","ODQP","MC","CN","QF","FR"];
    var BOX1  = ["BM","BN","BK","GNLK","KAML","CMLN"];
    var BOX2  = ["EQ","ER","EO","HRPO","ODQP","FQPR"];
    var ALL   = PYR.concat(SOLID, BOX1, BOX2);
    var ANG   = ALL.concat(["angABC","angDEF"]);
    var ANG2  = ANG.concat(["angGBC","angHEF"]);
    var ANG3  = ANG2.concat(["angABG","angDEH"]);
    var FAC   = ANG3.concat(["KGN","ACNK"]);
    var PRISM = ["ABC","KGN","BK","BN","ACNK"];
